KG42.register("clusters-df1625dbec80d8623312e6dc",{"id":"09-local_flexibility::v142-d-CL002","paper":"09-local_flexibility","label":"Service-delivery eligibility for target network elements","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Service-delivery eligibility for target network elements","market_meaning":"The DSO restricts the units eligible to deliver services according to the connectivity between the target network element and DER; capacity-limitation requests identify the applicable units through location information and the List of unit IDs, establishing eligibility boundaries at the service level.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The network-connectivity condition concerns the specific network element affected by the service; the provision in R002 explicitly using location information and a unit list is limited to capacity-limitation requests. Eligibility to deliver a particular service is not extended here into a uniform admission condition for the entire market.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"This chain already has the target network element and location information as conditions, designation of units by the DSO as the activity assigned to a responsible entity, and the scope of units eligible to deliver services as the result. It can independently constitute a procedural eligibility rule without being merged into economic clearing or information-confidentiality rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Jointly retains the network-location eligibility principle and its implementation through a unit list for capacity-limitation requests, with their scopes of applicability separately limited."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The unit list, network-connectivity relationships, and their verification process appear only in procedural prose, so the current chain cannot support automated eligibility calculation. This gap does not undermine the eligibility principle within this cluster's limited scope, but the generic admission.local_area node must not be used to derive a market-wide exclusion rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::admission.local_area","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If executable eligibility checks are required, the upstream layer should supply the basis for correspondence among services, unit IDs, and network connections, together with verification interfaces; retain the capacity-limitation subscope and the meaning of service-specific eligibility."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence used for the eligibility provisions remains unverified; assembled indicates only that the procedural candidate can be interpreted independently within the scope described above, not that the source text or scientific content has passed independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the network-location conditions, unit list, and product scope in the original text, maintaining the existing evidence status until the review is complete."}]},"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R002"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-19331a2875b03fea"]});
